From 4773208d54412f0f90cf1bcc4da0698aad4b5a58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dexq8 <dexq8@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:18:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: pause and flush capture on stop

Stopping a stream sends ASM_DATA_CMD_EOS in both directions. On the SM-T825
(Samsung's MSM8996 ADSP firmware), a capture stream that received EOS then
fails ASM_STREAM_CMD_CLOSE with ADSP_EFAILED, so re-preparing the PCM (as
PipeWire does between recordings) fails in a loop. Qualcomm's downstream
msm-pcm-q6-v2 never sends EOS to capture streams; it pauses and flushes
them. Do the same and keep EOS for playback.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

Notes:
    Testing: on 6.19.5 SM-T825 this lets PipeWire re-prepare a stopped capture
    stream, but repeated recording sessions are still not reliable (an occasional
    ASM_STREAM_CMD_CLOSE timeout remains), so this is a partial fix. On v7.3-rc7
    build-tested only (arm64, W=1).

 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 4f09fdd4090..1e1ca956d5d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -347,6 +347,20 @@ static int q6asm_dai_trigger(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 				       0, 0, 0);
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_STOP:
+		/*
+		 * EOS only makes sense for playback. Samsung's MSM8996 ADSP
+		 * then refuses to close a capture stream, so stop capture
+		 * like the downstream driver does: pause, then flush.
+		 */
+		if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
+			ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client,
+					       prtd->stream_id, CMD_PAUSE);
+			if (!ret)
+				ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client,
+						       prtd->stream_id,
+						       CMD_FLUSH);
+			break;
+		}
 		ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,
 				       CMD_EOS);
 		break;

